RT64 4337374 + plume d890ac8: present capture and widescreen fixes for the THPS1 recomp host
(apply after rt64-hlslpp-labs.patch).

  patch -p1 -d vendor/recomp-runtime/lib/rt64 < decomp/thps1/recomp-host/patches/rt64-present-capture-widescreen.patch

1. Present capture (PresentQueue::captureCallback / captureEvery / captureNext / captureWidth/Height):
   every Nth composited frame is drawn again by the VI renderer into an offscreen BGRA8 target
   (same input as the swap chain: resolved MSAA or downsampled target, VI scaling, filtering) and
   copied to a readback buffer; the callback gets the pixels on the present thread.
   PresentQueue::swapChainEnabled = false composites (and captures) without touching the swap
   chain (occluded or hidden windows). presentedFrameCount / windowPresentCount count frames.
   VIRenderer::RenderParams::targetWidth/Height lets the VI pass target something other than the
   swap chain. plume copyTextureRegion texture -> buffer (the readback), per backend:
     Metal   new branch (blit copyFromTexture): in use since Q16.
     D3D12   plume already converts a buffer footprint destination, but called setSamplePositions(dst.texture)
             first, which dereferences null for a buffer destination (Windows port, Q24): now takes the
             source texture when the destination is a buffer.
     Vulkan  the function had only buffer->image and image->image branches, so a buffer destination
             dereferenced null: new branch (vkCmdCopyImageToBuffer). (Q24)
   The D3D12 and Vulkan changes are written from the plume sources and compile, but have not run on
   hardware. The capture is only armed by --control / --present-dump-every / latency / edges
   (PresentQueue::captureEvery, captureNext), never in normal play.
2. Widescreen: a 1/32-width slack in the "covers the whole width" tests for wide viewports
   (FramebufferRenderer and ProjectionProcessor) and for full-width fill rects. THPS1 scissors
   its 3D and clears its depth buffer 8 px in from each side of a 320 px frame; without the slack
   its projection isn't widened (pillarbox) and the depth clear isn't stretched (the sides keep
   stale depth and stay black).
   RT64_DEBUG_WIDESCREEN=N logs the widening decision per projection every Nth pair.
3. (Q17) PresentQueue::captureUi: the render hook (RecompFrontend's recompui UI) is drawn into
   present captures too, and offscreen every frame while the swap chain is off, so menus keep
   updating in a hidden/occluded window and captures show them. Off unless the host sets it.
Patched lines are marked [thps-recomp].

